180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (The kerf test tool helped me evaluate how much extra material the laser removed and how that affects joint fit. At tighter tolerances, joints required noticeable force to assemble, which increased the risk of cracking. This test showed that laser power and material thickness directly affect fit, and that kerf compensation is necessary to achieve accurate press-fit joints rather than relying on nominal dimensions.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
